nctions  following uh russian troops crossing  into ukraine and and invading ukraine  this is what we heard here today and  some of them are blocking two russian  financial institutions cutting off  russia from the debt market so they  cannot refinance their sovereign debt  and then also targeting russian elites  families and this is actually the first  time  that president biden spoke about the  oligarchs and their connection to  vladimir putin so first tranche of  sanctions but it's also important to  point out here that there will be more  and can be more should vladimir putin  decide to escalate the situation further  what are people saying about how much of  an impact these sanctions will really  have  yeah that's really the big question  because of course this is not a surprise  for vladimir putin and for russia and  they've had a lot of time uh in thinking  about exactly this question it's  certainly a first step it's a dramatic  one russia sees now from the perspective  of the white house that they have to pay  a price for their actions it also leaves  the door open for vladimir putin because  there are more sanctions to come only if  putin decides that he wants to attack  ukraine further that he wants to move  his troops  beyond the separatist controlled areas  so there's still of course a chance for  him to steer back or to decide for a  diplomatic path but of course the u.s  expectation is  not as optimistic anymore  the problem is of course that vladimir  putin might have factored all that in  already  alvaro how likely is the u.s government  to launch further measures against  russia i suppose that has a lot to do  with what russia does  yeah that's just right michael it really  depends on what's going to happen next  just to just keep in mind there will be  no military intervention um ukraine is  not a nato member so we're talking about  further sanctions and that really  depends on the question will russia move  their troops beyond the separatist  con