 territories  the separatist controlled territories um  these uh self-proclaimed republics  control about a third a fourth to a  third of the territory of these two  uh uh terri of these two districts of  ukraine um including both capitals  district capitals but uh and and some  areas around but vast uh parts of these  districts are under ukrainian government  control and he now makes claims to these  territories this makes of course a  military action to gain control of these  territories more probable there has been  some confusion about this yesterday  however this is not unexpected and as we  heard yesterday that putin basically  claims the whole of ukraine as part of  russia  how are people taking this where you are  in in the donetsk region  we've seen in this region  an escalation of violence during the  fast past five days and the lead up to  this decision  mostly what we've seen is shelling from  the separatist side onto villages  controlled by the ukrainian army and  also onto military posts but a lot of  civilian villages as well  so  people here are of course scared of an  escalation have been scared of an  escalation for some time this of course  makes it even more probable that this  escalation will really come and it will  happen here in this area today i went to  one of these villages and the people  that have been basically sitting in  their basement for for for five days now  they're really scared of what's  happening many people are escaping right  now people mostly are escaping from the  front line from these villages that are  being shelled but of course all over the  place and here in the city that 70  kilometers from the line um fear is  growing  fear scared and also no doubt looking to  see how their government is reacting can  you tell us how the ukrainian government  is responding to the threat from russia  up until now the ukrainian government  has been very measured very restrained  they have of course said that this does  not make sense 